{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — 07 THE REGISTER.
  Wireframe (01) HOMEPAGE §07: dark field, headline left, invitation and form right.

  Terminology (CLAUDE.md, non-negotiable): this is The Register — public and free to
  join. The Circle is invitation-only and has no public form, so nothing here may
  offer one. The Dispatch is the newsletter The Register receives.

  Why this is not Luxe's native `newsletter`: that section has no eyebrow, and it
  places the invitation copy in the heading column rather than above the form. The
  form itself is still Shopify's own customer form — same submission,
  same success and error states, same customer record.

  Klaviyo (14 Sep): the form below posts to Klaviyo directly, from the theme's
  own markup, via assets/ha-klaviyo-form.js. The embedded Klaviyo form could not
  be made to match the design without keeping the palette in two places, so the
  design stays here and only the destination changed. Company and list IDs live
  in theme settings; the one thing set per placement is `register_source`, which
  is what lets Aloha see which call to action actually works. With JS off it is
  still Shopify's customer form and the Shopify → Klaviyo sync catches it.

  The @app block slot is kept as the fallback — if it is ever used again,
  switch "Show the Shopify form" off so two forms are never live at once.

  `novalidate` so the script draws the invalid states rather than the browser's
  bubble. `data-nocaptcha` because Shopify's storefront captcha bootstrap binds
  every /contact customer form and, once bound, calls form.submit() itself on
  submit — straight past our preventDefault and onto the /challenge page. That
  attribute is its own documented opt-out. With JS off, Shopify still
  challenges server-side, so nothing is weakened.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section id="the-register" class="ha-section ha-section--dark ha-register">
  <div class="ha-wrap">
    <div class="ha-register__grid">
      <div>
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-eyebrow ha-record">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="ha-display ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          WHERE THE INVITATION COPY SITS.

          On the homepage it belongs under the heading it explains, rather than
          stacked above the form in the opposite column — that was the call on
          3 September and it stands.

          Aloha's Circle design places it the other way: heading alone on the
          left, the paragraph directly above the email field on the right. Both
          readings are right for their own page, so this is a setting rather
          than a rewrite. The default keeps the homepage exactly as approved.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.body != blank and section.settings.body_position != 'form' -%}
          <div class="ha-body ha-narrate ha-register__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="ha-register__aside">

        {%- if section.settings.body != blank and section.settings.body_position == 'form' -%}
          <div class="ha-body ha-narrate ha-register__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- case block.type -%}
            {%- when '@app' -%}
              {% render block %}
          {%- endcase -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_native_form -%}
          {%- form 'customer',
            class: 'ha-register__form newsletter-form',
            novalidate: 'novalidate',
            data-nocaptcha: 'true',
            data-ha-klaviyo: '',
            data-company-id: settings.ha_klaviyo_company_id,
            data-list-id: settings.ha_klaviyo_register_list,
            data-source: section.settings.register_source,
            data-msg-invalid: section.settings.msg_invalid,
            data-msg-consent: section.settings.msg_consent,
            data-msg-submitting: section.settings.msg_submitting,
            data-msg-success: section.settings.msg_success,
            data-msg-error: section.settings.msg_error
          -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ section.settings.contact_tag }}">

            {%- comment -%}
              One live region for every state the script can reach — invalid,
              consent, submitting, success, error. Shopify's own messages below
              only render on the no-JS round trip.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="ha-register__message ha-record" data-ha-form-status tabindex="-1" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>

            <div class="ha-register__field">
              <label class="ha-register__label ha-record" for="HaRegister--{{ section.id }}">
                {{ 'newsletter.label' | t }}
              </label>
              <input
                id="HaRegister--{{ section.id }}"
                type="email"
                name="contact[email]"
                class="ha-register__input ha-narrate"
                value="{{ form.email }}"
                aria-required="true"
                autocorrect="off"
                autocapitalize="off"
                autocomplete="email"
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.email_placeholder | escape }}"
                {% if form.errors %}
                  aria-invalid="true"
                  aria-describedby="HaRegister-error--{{ section.id }}"
                {% elsif form.posted_successfully? %}
                  aria-describedby="HaRegister-success--{{ section.id }}"
                {% endif %}
                required
              >
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The button sits OUTSIDE the field. Nested inside it, the field's
              underline ran beneath the button too and the two read as one
              control; the design has a single rule under the input, then space,
              then the solid button.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Express consent, never pre-ticked. CASL applies — the entity is in
              British Columbia — so this is a legal requirement, not a style.
              The wording is Christina's and ships as a labelled placeholder
              until it lands.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <label class="ha-register__consent ha-narrate">
              <input type="checkbox" data-ha-consent required aria-required="true">
              <span>{{ section.settings.consent_text }}</span>
            </label>

            <button type="submit" class="ha-register__submit ha-identify" name="commit">
              {{ 'newsletter.button_label' | t }}
            </button>

            {%- if form.errors -%}
              <p class="ha-register__message ha-record" id="HaRegister-error--{{ section.id }}" role="alert">
                {{- form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages.email -}}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
              <p class="ha-register__message ha-record" id="HaRegister-success--{{ section.id }}" tabindex="-1" role="status">
                {{- 'newsletter.success' | t -}}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endform -%}
          <script src="{{ 'ha-klaviyo-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — The Register",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "email_placeholder", "label": "Email placeholder", "default": "you@example.com" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The Register" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Be first to receive what comes next." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Invitation", "default": "<p>Private access to new Lots, The Dispatch, and stories from the workshops before they reach the wider world.</p>" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "body_position", "label": "Invitation sits", "default": "heading",
      "info": "The homepage keeps it under the heading. The Circle page places it above the email field, as Aloha's design draws it.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "heading", "label": "Under the heading (left)" },
        { "value": "form", "label": "Above the email field (right)" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_native_form", "label": "Show the form", "default": true, "info": "This form posts to Klaviyo. Switch off only if a Klaviyo app block is carrying the form instead — never both." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "contact_tag", "label": "Customer tag (no-JS fallback only)", "default": "the-register" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Klaviyo" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "register_source", "label": "Source", "default": "homepage_band",
      "info": "Recorded on the profile as register_source, one value per placement — this is what answers 'which call to action worked'.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "homepage_band", "label": "Homepage band" },
        { "value": "footer", "label": "Footer" },
        { "value": "product_page", "label": "Product page" },
        { "value": "circle_page", "label": "The Circle page" },
        { "value": "about_page", "label": "About page" },
        { "value": "collection_page", "label": "Collection page" },
        { "value": "journal", "label": "Journal" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext", "id": "consent_text", "label": "Consent line",
      "default": "<p>[PLACEHOLDER — wording from Christina] Yes, add me to The Register. I can leave at any time.</p>",
      "info": "Required to submit and never pre-ticked. The wording is a legal matter under CASL — Aloha to confirm with Christina."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Messages" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_invalid", "label": "Invalid email", "default": "Please enter a valid email address." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_consent", "label": "Consent not ticked", "default": "Please tick the box to join." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_submitting", "label": "While sending", "default": "One moment…" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_success", "label": "Success", "default": "Thank you. A confirmation is on its way — one click and you are on The Register.", "info": "The list is double opt-in, so the success message must send them to their inbox." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_error", "label": "Service error", "default": "That did not go through. Please try again, or write to contact@hartwickatelier.com." }
  ],
  "blocks": [{ "type": "@app" }],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Hartwick — The Register" }]
}
{% endschema %}
